<Application x:Class="Crystal.Controls.Demo.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             StartupUri="AllControlsWindow.xaml">
  <!--
    Every Control this demo uses resolves its default look through Crystal.Controls's own
    Themes/Generic.xaml (PerformanceGraphView, RangeBarView, LoadingHost, the scrollbar style),
    which WPF auto-applies to any control from that assembly without this app merging anything -
    that's what ResourceDictionaryLocation.SourceAssembly in Crystal.Controls's AssemblyInfo.cs is
    for.

    PerformanceGraphLite is different: it's a plain FrameworkElement, not a Control, so it never
    gets Generic.xaml's automatic DefaultStyleKey fallback no matter what ResourceDictionaryLocation
    says - that mechanism is Control-only. The merge below is what actually makes
    Themes/PerformanceGraphLiteStyles.xaml's no-key style apply, and it's a real behavior change,
    not just wiring, for AllControlsWindow.xaml's "LiteDefault" tile: it sets no local
    ColorMode/Color1..Color9, so it renders this style's ramp instead of Crystal.Controls's own
    internal default ramp (see the comment on that tile). PerformanceGraphMultipleDS's Lite1/Lite2
    equivalents - CpuSeries/RamSeries/GpuSeries in the same window - aren't PerformanceGraphLite at
    all, so this merge doesn't apply to them regardless.
  -->
  <Application.Resources>
    <ResourceDictionary>
      <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Themes/PerformanceGraphLiteStyles.xaml"/>
        <!-- Keyed-only (SquareGridPerformanceGraphStyle) - merging this has no automatic effect
             on anything, unlike the no-key style above, since a keyed style only applies where
             explicitly referenced via Style="{StaticResource ...}". -->
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Themes/PerformanceGraphSquareGridStyles.xaml"/>
      </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
    </ResourceDictionary>
  </Application.Resources>
</Application>
